  Architecture Review & Gap Analysis: account_tca_peppol                                                                                                                                                                                                                       
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  1. Architecture Decision: You Made the Right Call                                                                                                                                                                                                                            
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  Your choice to follow the PEPPOL pattern (Send & Print wizard) rather than the ZATCA pattern (legacy EDI framework) is correct for these reasons:                                                                                                                            
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  - The legacy account.edi.format + account.edi.document framework is being phased out in Odoo 18+                                                                                                                                                                             
  - You don't need the chain integrity mechanism ZATCA requires (no ICV, no hash chain, no XAdES signing)                                                                                                                                                                      
  - The Send & Print wizard gives you user-initiated control, which is appropriate since UAE e-invoicing doesn't require automatic submission on posting (unlike ZATCA which auto-submits)                                                                                     
  - Your webhook-first + cron-fallback approach is architecturally superior to both PEPPOL (cron-only polling) and ZATCA (cron-only processing)                                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
  One architectural concern: You declared 'conflicts': ['account_peppol'] in the manifest. This is correct for UAE businesses, but consider: a multi-national company running Odoo might need account_peppol for their European entities AND your module for UAE entities. The 
  conflict prevents this. Since you use a completely separate state machine (tca_move_state vs peppol_move_state) and separate wizard fields (checkbox_send_tca vs checkbox_send_peppol), there's no actual technical conflict — only the                                      
  _call_web_service_after_invoice_pdf_render override chain. Both call super() first, so they'd coexist. Consider removing the conflict and testing coexistence.                                                                                                               
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
